# The language bar should describe what this project is, not be tuned until it
# flatters. Python is the tool; YAML is the action, the hook and the workflows,
# which are a real part of what this repository ships and stay counted.
*.md linguist-documentation
docs/** linguist-documentation
*.sarif linguist-generated

# The fixtures are the one place an explicit decision is needed. They are Sigma
# rules I wrote to be wrong in one specific way each: inputs to the tests
# rather than content this project maintains. Linguist has no Sigma, so left
# alone they would read as a tenth of this repository being YAML written by its
# author. Marked not detectable rather than vendored, because vendored would
# claim they came from somewhere else and they did not.
tests/fixtures/** linguist-detectable=false
